schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Verra banned tokenizing already-retired carbon credits (2023)"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In 2023 the standards body Verra banned converting already-retired
    carbon credits into tokens, after critics showed many tokenized credits
    were tied to old, low-quality projects that weren't genuinely helping
    the climate; the industry is now working toward an "immobilize, don't
    double-count" approach instead.
  evidence: >-
    Stated in the source article as historical/regulatory context for
    Toucan and the broader carbon-tokenization space; article links to
    Toucan's own blog response to Verra's announcement as a reference.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/what-is-refi.md
  interpretation: >-
    Article uses this as its central "honest part" — the concrete
    greenwashing cautionary example backing its claim that "tokenizing
    something does not automatically make it good."
  uncertainty: >-
    Presented from the source article's summary and Toucan's own
    response-to-Verra post (one interested party's framing); the underlying
    Verra policy text and independent reporting on the episode were not
    reviewed directly here.
  high_risk: true
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-is-refi.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
